6: 
7: # Tracker Governance Contract
8: 
9: This document defines how planning trackers stay current and trustworthy.
10: 
11: ## Why This Exists
12: 
13: - `REGISTRY.md`, `ROADMAP.md`, `STORY-INDEX.md`, `BLUEPRINT.md`, and per-feature `STATUS.md` are operational controls.
14: - Feature/story state transitions must update tracker state in the same change set.
15: 
16: ## Authoritative Tracker Roles
17: 
18: - `{PRODUCT_ROOT}/planning-mds/features/REGISTRY.md`: authoritative feature inventory, status, and folder paths. (In a compiled-projection repo, the feature **tables** are generated fenced regions from the feature shards via `tracker_gen.py`; the surrounding prose stays authored.)
19: - `{PRODUCT_ROOT}/planning-mds/features/ROADMAP.md`: authoritative sequencing view (`Now / Next / Later / Completed`).
20: - `{PRODUCT_ROOT}/planning-mds/features/STORY-INDEX.md`: auto-generated story rollup from strict story filenames.
21: - `{PRODUCT_ROOT}/planning-mds/features/F{NNNN}-{slug}/STATUS.md`: authoritative feature execution state and deferred follow-ups.
22: - `{PRODUCT_ROOT}/planning-mds/BLUEPRINT.md`: baseline strategy snapshot; must not contradict tracker state.
23: 
24: ## Ownership
25: 
26: - Product Manager: updates tracker docs during planning changes.
27: - Architect: validates tracker consistency at planning-to-build handoff. Owns the required signoff matrix at planning time — sets which roles are mandatory for each feature's completion.
28: - Implementers: update feature `STATUS.md` when story state changes.
29: - Code Reviewer: blocks approval when tracker drift is detected.
30: - Quality Engineer: validates acceptance criteria coverage and records test signoff evidence.
31: - Security Reviewer: records security signoff when included in required signoff roles.
32: 
33: ## Signoff Governance (Mandatory)
34: 
35: - Every feature `STATUS.md` must include:
36:   - `Required Signoff Roles`
37:   - `Story Signoff Provenance`
38: - Minimum required roles for features marked `Done` or moved to archive:
39:   - `Quality Engineer`
40:   - `Code Reviewer`
41: - Architect adds additional required roles based on risk/scope:
42:   - `Security Reviewer` — for authn/authz, access control, identity/session, secrets, sensitive data boundaries, or policy changes
43:   - `DevOps` — for runtime/deployability or environment-contract changes
44:   - `Architect` — when architecture-sensitive exceptions or tradeoffs require explicit acceptance
45: - Every required role must have story-level provenance entries for every story in scope with:
46:   - pass verdict (`PASS` or `APPROVED`)
47:   - reviewer identity
48:   - review date
49:   - concrete evidence path(s)
50: - Product Manager must not close or archive a feature until all required signoffs pass.
51: 
52: ## Provenance Boundary Rules (Mandatory)
53: 
54: - Signoff provenance is solution execution evidence and must live outside `agents/`.
55: - `agents/**` may define process/templates/checklists, but is never accepted as completion evidence.
56: - Provenance `Evidence` should point to project outputs such as:
57:   - `{PRODUCT_ROOT}/planning-mds/**` (reviews, test plans, security evidence, tracker updates)
58:   - implementation/test artifacts in `{PRODUCT_ROOT}/engine/**`, `{PRODUCT_ROOT}/experience/**`, `{PRODUCT_ROOT}/neuron/**`, `docs/**`, or CI outputs
59: 
60: ## Lifecycle Rules
61: 
62: - Feature lifecycle states: `Draft` -> `In Progress` -> `Done` -> `Archived`.
63: - `Done` means implementation complete and signoff evidence captured in `STATUS.md`.
64: - `Done` may include a `Deferred Non-Blocking Follow-ups` section in `STATUS.md`; deferments must not change overall completion state.
65: - Archived features must:
66:   - live under `{PRODUCT_ROOT}/planning-mds/features/archive/`
67:   - be listed under `Archived Features` in `REGISTRY.md`
68:   - appear in `ROADMAP.md` under `Completed`, not `Now/Next/Later`.
69: 
70: ## Orphaned Story Rule (Mandatory)
71: 
72: Before marking a feature `Done` or moving to `Archived`, the PM must verify that all non-completed stories are either:
73: 
74: 1. **Explicitly deferred** in `STATUS.md` `Deferred Non-Blocking Follow-ups` with a tracking link to a new or existing feature, or
75: 2. **Promoted** to a new feature ID in `REGISTRY.md` if the scope warrants standalone tracking.
76: 
77: No story file may be archived in a `Not Started` or `In Progress` state without a rehoming decision recorded in the closeout. This prevents future work from being silently buried in the archive.
78: 
79: ## Story File Rules
80: 
81: - Story files must follow `F{NNNN}-S{NNNN}-{slug}.md`.
82: - Non-story documents in feature folders must not start with `F{NNNN}-S{NNNN}`.
83: - Story IDs in file content must match filename prefix.
84: 
85: ## Mandatory Sync Triggers
86: 
87: Update trackers immediately when any of the following occurs:
88: 
89: 1. A feature is created, renamed, moved, or archived.
90: 2. A story is added, removed, renamed, or moved.
91: 3. A feature/story status changes (including done/archive transitions).
92: 4. Roadmap prioritization or sequencing changes.
93: 5. Blueprint feature/story status text changes.
94: 
95: ## Required Validation Commands
96: 
97: Run these before declaring planning or feature execution complete:
98: 
99: ```bash
100: python3 agents/product-manager/scripts/validate-stories.py {PRODUCT_ROOT}/planning-mds/features/F{NNNN}-{slug}/
101: python3 agents/product-manager/scripts/generate-story-index.py {PRODUCT_ROOT}/planning-mds/features/
102: python3 agents/product-manager/scripts/validate-trackers.py
103: ```
104: 
105: ## Definition of Fresh Trackers
106: 
107: All conditions must pass:
108: 
109: - [ ] Every `REGISTRY.md` folder path exists and points to the correct active/archive location.
110: - [ ] `ROADMAP.md` links resolve and align with current feature state.
111: - [ ] `STORY-INDEX.md` story count and links match current strict story files.
112: - [ ] `BLUEPRINT.md` linked feature/story paths resolve and match archive status.
113: - [ ] No non-story file is parsed as a story.
114: - [ ] For every feature in `Done` or `Archived`, required signoff roles have story-level passing provenance evidence for each story in `STATUS.md`.
115: 
116: ## Feature Evidence Contract
117: 
118: Done / Archived governed features must cite canonical feature evidence package files, not broad solution artifacts:
119: 
120: - Story signoff `Evidence` paths must resolve under `{PRODUCT_ROOT}/planning-mds/operations/evidence/runs/{RUN_ID}/...`.
121: - The feature index root must carry an approved `latest-run.json`.
122: - `validate-trackers.py` calls `validate-feature-evidence.py --stage G6` after tracker validation; final `G8`/`closeout` validation runs by the closeout action after tracker results are logged. This non-circular sequence is mandatory.
123: - Retired features (`Terminal Status = Abandoned` or `Superseded`) are registry-only and never satisfy completion-evidence requirements.
124: - Product effective-date baseline: governed completed-terminal features closed or archived on or after `2026-05-19` require canonical feature evidence. Pre-contract archived features are skipped unless an `Evidence Reentry Date` on or after `2026-05-19` is present.


