FILE: planning-mds/examples/personas/security-administrator.md
1: # Persona: Noor the Security Administrator
2: 
3: **Role/Title:** Identity and access administrator for the Nebula Insurance Brain deployment
4: **Archetype:** Internal platform user — operates the identity provider, sessions, principals and grants (master blueprint §1.2, §65, §66)
5: **Priority:** Secondary (F0021); primary for F0026 AuthX hardening
6: 
7: ## Demographics & Background
8: 
9: **Experience Level:** 8+ years running enterprise SSO and access reviews; reads audit trails daily
10: **Technical Proficiency:** High for identity tooling and logs; not a frontend developer
11: **Daily Responsibilities:**
12: - Provision and disable users and service clients at the identity provider
13: - Revoke grants and confirm the revocation took effect
14: - Investigate failed sign-ins, credential stuffing and unusual session activity
15: 
16: ## Goals & Motivations
17: 
18: ### Primary Goals
19: 1. Know that no browser holds a reusable token: a stolen laptop or a script injected into the page cannot lift a refresh token (ADR-0051 D5)
20: 2. Know that "signed out" means the upstream session and refresh token are revoked, and be told when that failed (ADR-0051 D4)
21: 3. Keep audit storage bounded when an attacker floods bad credentials (F0002 carry-in)
22: 
23: ### Success Metrics
24: - Zero tokens found in browser storage during review; every logout has a recorded upstream outcome; rejected-credential rows stay within the configured bound per client per window
25: 
26: ## Pain Points & Frustrations
27: 
28: 1. **Logout that only clears a cookie** — Impact: a refresh token keeps working upstream; Frequency: every logout; Severity: Critical
29: 2. **Audit tables flooded by bad-credential bursts** — Impact: storage growth and noisy investigations; Frequency: during attacks; Severity: High
30: 3. **UI-only session timeouts** — Impact: a modal is dismissed and the server session lives on; Frequency: daily; Severity: High
31: 
32: ## Jobs-to-be-Done
33: 
34: 1. **When** I disable a user or revoke a grant, **I want to** see the next request refused, **so I can** close an incident with evidence.
35: 2. **When** a logout cannot reach the identity provider, **I want to** find a recorded failure, **so I can** revoke the session manually.
36: 3. **When** one address floods bad credentials, **I want to** see it throttled with one summary event per window, **so I can** investigate without wading through thousands of rows.
37: 
38: ## Constraints & Considerations
39: 
40: - Authorization: administers the identity provider and policy releases; holds no special data-read authority inside Nebula through the shell.
41: - Does not use the shell for administration in v0.1; evidence comes from audit rows and logs.
42: 
43: ## Related Features
44: 
45: F0021 (session, logout, throttling), F0026 (retention, production ingress, AuthX negative tests).

